<p>In the latest turn, the United States and Iran agreed to a conditional two-week ceasefire just before President Donald Trump’s deadline for Tehran to reopen the Strait of Hormuz or face broader US attacks. Multiple outlets said Israel also backed the pause. Iranian officials said safe passage through Hormuz would be allowed during the truce, and several reports said direct or indirect negotiations are expected to begin in Islamabad on April 10 after Pakistani mediation helped secure the deal. The agreement brought immediate relief to global markets, with oil prices falling sharply and stocks rising on hopes that one of the world’s most important energy shipping lanes will reopen more fully. The truce followed hours of intense uncertainty after President Trump threatened major strikes on Iranian civilian infrastructure and warned that “a whole civilization will die tonight.” Those remarks drew criticism from international legal experts, the pope, and some US lawmakers before he announced the pause. Even after the ceasefire announcement, major questions remained about its scope and durability: Iran and the United States each cast the outcome as a win, Iran’s reported 10-point negotiating proposal includes demands such as sanctions relief and acceptance of uranium enrichment, and Israeli officials said the ceasefire does not apply to Lebanon.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/qJv7rBdJNb7LBJqYJbjrmKez6t-HTo1negwUF7rrSUBeH7zW9i0KvejTkCy-vqloGHyQY6A1De6vcZ_0lscYVsFVP8RSqF0mC7e3bu1Sq0U7vIbeKLUiVQJghfBvJk5qrXcznQHYbawTZGftpI8xf4Ra-Dby-A59-f4ioNPBuKwx2mBAbD-WylffoLtr3_KwWl1rHZEDxBRZ7uqno99nvfWIJuXMBWaMc4oIDP6CaSVVYlVLs6vRbchi9-Iedx2y5rFB3NNapOqPYZMbMg' alt='An anti-war demonstrator holds a peace sign near the White House during protests over the Iran war on April 7, 2026, in Washington, D.C.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Pakistan’s role: President Trump said he agreed to suspend attacks after speaking with Pakistani Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif and Field Marshal Asim Munir, while Islamabad invited both sides to talks on April 10.</li><li>Shaky start: Within hours of the truce, Bahrain sounded a missile alert, and Israeli media reports cited by multiple outlets said missiles had been fired from Iran, underscoring how fragile the pause remains.</li><li>US politics: Reaction in Washington split along partisan lines. Republican Iran hawks voiced skepticism about talks, while Democrats welcomed the ceasefire but sought accountability for the President’s earlier rhetoric.</li><li>Regional relief: Reports from Iraq described celebrations after the announcement, reflecting broader public hope that a wider regional war might still be avoided.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Iran: Iranian officials cast the ceasefire as a victory, arguing that Washington’s acceptance of a two-week pause and Tehran’s proposal as a basis for talks showed the US had stepped back from escalation. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/both-sides-claim-victory-after-us-iran-agree-to-11th-hour-truce'>The Straits Times</a>, <a href='https://www.rt.com/news/637638-trump-iran-ceacefire-extension/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Israel: Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said Israel backs the US pause while maintaining that Iran must no longer pose a nuclear, missile, or “terror” threat to Israel, the United States, or Arab neighbours. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israel-backs-trumps-two-week-pause-on-iran-strikes-says-lebanon-excluded/article70837139.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Pope Leo XIV: The pope called President Trump’s threat against Iranian civilian infrastructure “truly unacceptable” and urged leaders to return to the table and reject war. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/04/07/pope-leo-condemns-trumps-latest-threats-against-iran-00862464'>Politico</a>)</li><li>UN human rights chief: Volker Türk warned that deliberate attacks on civilians and civilian infrastructure are war crimes and criticized the incendiary rhetoric surrounding the conflict. (<a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-04-07-0700/donald-trump-un-chief-decries-incendiary-rhetoric-after-trump-ramps-threats-against-iran-deal-deadline-looms'>AllSides</a>)</li><li>US experts: PBS interviews with Alan Eyre and Miad Maleki highlighted sharply different readings of Tehran’s leverage, showing a live debate over whether the ceasefire strengthens diplomacy or buys Iran time. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/mideast-experts-weigh-iran-regimes-leverage-in-negotiations-with-u-s'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/07/2026/trumps-iran-deadline-looms'>Trump agrees to suspend Iran attacks for two weeks</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/USA/Politics/2026/0407/trump-iran-threat-brinksmanship-deadline'>Two-week ceasefire with Iran highlights Trump’s verbal brinkmanship</a> - csmonitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/637638-trump-iran-ceacefire-extension/'>Trump walks back threat to destroy Iranian civilization</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/08/trump-agrees-to-suspend-attack-on-iran-by-two-weeks_6752201_4.html'>Trump agrees to a two-week ceasefire with Iran</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.economist.com/middle-east-and-africa/2026/04/08/iran-and-america-agree-to-pause-their-war'>Iran and America agree to pause their war</a> - economist.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/08/us-and-iran-agree-to-two-week-truce-after-trump-pulls-back-on-threats'>US and Iran agree to two-week truce after Trump pulls back on threats</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/13578e0f-7218-4a80-b824-ac4ad318f860'>FirstFT: Trump and Iran announce 2-week ceasefire</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-04-08/the-united-states-and-iran-agree-to-a-twoweek-ceasefire-just-before-trumps-deadlin